From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] html: boxes with opacity 0 are not drawn

NetSurf has no opacity: a box with opacity: 0 (and everything in it) was
drawn as if opaque, so the hover and focus layers that pages keep
invisible with opacity: 0 covered the page (YouTube's results became
black blocks once their var() colours resolved).  Such boxes are now
skipped; other opacities are still drawn opaque.
---
 netsurf/content/handlers/html/redraw.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/netsurf/content/handlers/html/redraw.c b/netsurf/content/handlers/html/redraw.c
index f770699..1566fa9 100644
--- a/netsurf/content/handlers/html/redraw.c
+++ b/netsurf/content/handlers/html/redraw.c
@@ -1253,6 +1253,15 @@ bool html_redraw_box(const html_content *html, struct box *box,
 	if (html_redraw_printing && (box->flags & PRINTED))
 		return true;
 
+	/* a box with opacity: 0 is not seen, nor is anything in it (other
+	 * opacities are drawn opaque: there is no compositing) */
+	if (box->style != NULL) {
+		css_fixed opacity = INTTOFIX(1);
+		if (css_computed_opacity(box->style, &opacity) ==
+				CSS_OPACITY_SET && opacity <= 0)
+			return true;
+	}
+
 	if (box->style != NULL) {
 		overflow_x = css_computed_overflow_x(box->style);
 		overflow_y = css_computed_overflow_y(box->style);
